🐛 Describe the bug
Root cause of #109138
Reproducer:
import torch

def cool_name(x):
    return x.sin()

def fn(x):
    return torch.no_grad(cool_name)(x)

x = torch.zeros(10)
result = fn(x)
print(result)
result = torch.compile(fn, backend="eager", fullgraph=True)(x)
print(result)
Also fails:
def fn(x):
    @torch.no_grad
    def cool_name(x):
        return x.sin()

    return cool_name(x)

x = torch.zeros(10)
result = fn(x)
print(result)
result = torch.compile(fn, backend="eager", fullgraph=True)(x)
print(result)
Does not fail: no_grad is instantiated outside of compile region
@torch.no_grad
def cool_name(x):
    return x.sin()

def fn(x):
    return cool_name(x)

x = torch.zeros(10)
result = fn(x)
print(result)
result = torch.compile(fn, backend="eager", fullgraph=True)(x)
print(result)
Solution
Handle it properly when it is called as a function. It might need to instantiate the gradmodevariable whenever the function is called.
To do so, one can put a context_var_hook which sets up the context var when the function is called.
